// Class 12 English Core - Flamingo Poetry Chapter 12: A Roadside Stand
// Fully standardized to English Core Blueprint & AGENTS.md guidelines

export const c12EngF12HtmlOverview = "\n<div style=\"padding: 18px; color: #F8FAFC; text-align: justify; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif; line-height: 1.85; font-size: 15px;\">\n  <!-- Chapter Header Badge -->\n  <div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.18), rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.95)); border: 1.5px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 14px; padding: 22px; margin-bottom: 24px; box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);\">\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 10px;\">\n      <span style=\"background: #FF9100; color: #0F172A; font-weight: 800; font-size: 12px; padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 6px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">Poem 12 • Flamingo Poetry</span>\n      <span style=\"color: #94A3B8; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600;\">Core Literature • Class 12 English</span>\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 26px; font-weight: 800; margin: 0 0 8px 0; letter-spacing: -0.5px;\">A Roadside Stand</h1>\n    <p style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 12px 0;\">By Robert Frost (1874–1963) • Four-Time Pulitzer Prize Winner</p>\n    <p style=\"color: #CBD5E1; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;\">A searing, compassionate social commentary depicting the economic anguish, shattered dignity, and vain hopes of impoverished rural folk contrasted against the calloused indifference of wealthy city travellers and manipulative political benefactors.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Poet Background & Context -->\n  <div style=\"background: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.7); border-left: 4px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0; padding: 18px 20px; margin-bottom: 24px;\">\n    <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700;\">1. About the Poet & Societal Reality</h3>\n    <p style=\"margin: 0 0 10px 0;\">Robert Frost was an iconic American poet celebrated for his realistic depictions of rural New England life, deceptively conversational diction, and deep philosophical insight. While famous for poems of pastoral nature, Frost was acutely sensitive to the human tragedies wrought by industrial urbanization, capitalist disparity, and political exploitation.</p>\n    <p style=\"margin: 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">Context of the Poem:</b> <i style=\"color: #FF9100;\">A Roadside Stand</i> portrays the growing gulf between booming American metropolitan centers and decaying rural settlements. Frost articulates the raw, unadorned sorrow of roadside peasants who plead not for degrading charitable alms, but for fair commercial exchange and a dignified share of the national prosperity flowing along the asphalt highways.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Stanza-by-Stanza Deep Analysis -->\n  <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; margin-bottom: 24px;\">\n    <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; margin: 0 0 16px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700;\">2. Stanza-by-Stanza Critical Analysis</h3>\n    \n    <div style=\"margin-bottom: 16px; padding-bottom: 14px; border-bottom: 1px dashed rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">\n      <h4 style=\"color: #F1F5F9; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">Stanza 1: The Pathetic Plea of the Roadside Shed</b></h4>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0; color: #CBD5E1; font-size: 14px;\">An impoverished country household erects a humble new wooden shed attached to their old house right by the speeding highway. Personified by Frost, <i style=\"color: #FFFFFF;\">\"A roadside stand that too pathetically pled\"</i> does not beg for a humiliating <i style=\"color: #FFFFFF;\">\"dole of bread\"</i> (charity). Instead, the peasants yearn for honest cash—the very liquid capital that sustains metropolitan opulence and prevents the <i style=\"color: #FFFFFF;\">\"flower of cities from sinking and withering faint.\"</i> However, the wealthy speeding motorists (<i style=\"color: #FFFFFF;\">\"polished traffic\"</i>) drive past with cold detachment, complaining only that the crude shed and backward directional signs ('N' and 'S' painted wrong) mar the pristine landscape.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div style=\"margin-bottom: 16px; padding-bottom: 14px; border-bottom: 1px dashed rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">\n      <h4 style=\"color: #F1F5F9; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">Stanza 2: The Grievance & Hollywood Cinema Promises</b></h4>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0; color: #CBD5E1; font-size: 14px;\">The stand offers humble country produce: wooden quarts of wild mountain berries and crook-necked golden squash with silver warts. When passing motorists scold them crossly for marring scenic beauty, the owners harbor a deep, silent wound: <i style=\"color: #FFFFFF;\">\"the sorrow of what is unsaid.\"</i> They seek enough city money to experience life's expansion—the luxurious living standard promised by Hollywood moving pictures, which the entrenched political party in power cynically denies them.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div style=\"margin-bottom: 16px; padding-bottom: 14px; border-bottom: 1px dashed rgba(255,255,255,0.1);\">\n      <h4 style=\"color: #F1F5F9; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">Stanza 3: Exploitative Philanthropy & Paternalistic Greed</b></h4>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0; color: #CBD5E1; font-size: 14px;\">The poet bitterly notes government announcements proclaiming that these <i style=\"color: #FFFFFF;\">\"pitiful kin\"</i> (destitute villagers) will be relocated into compact settlements adjacent to suburban cinema halls and supermarkets. Frost unmasks this alleged benevolence as predatory exploitation: corrupt politicians and real estate tycoons act as <i style=\"color: #FFFFFF;\">\"greedy good-doers, beneficent beasts of prey.\"</i> By enforcing superficial welfare programs, they lull the peasants into lethargy (<i style=\"color: #FFFFFF;\">\"soothe them out of their wits\"</i>), eroding their ancestral self-reliance and destroying their traditional working rhythms.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div>\n      <h4 style=\"color: #F1F5F9; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">Stanza 4: The Agony of Vain Longing & Frost's Moral Dilemma</b></h4>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0; color: #CBD5E1; font-size: 14px;\">Frost admits he can scarcely bear the heartbreak of their <i style=\"color: #FFFFFF;\">\"childish longing in vain.\"</i> An open window waits all day in mute prayer for the screech of braking tires. Yet, of the thousands of <i style=\"color: #FFFFFF;\">\"selfish cars\"</i>, the rare few that pull over do so merely to turn around on the grass, ask directions, or demand petrol that the peasants obviously cannot supply. In a moment of overwhelming sorrow, Frost confesses that putting these suffering folk out of their misery <i style=\"color: #FFFFFF;\">\"at one stroke\"</i> would offer instant relief, before quickly recoiling the next day, realizing that such rash thoughts violate human empathy and moral sanity.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Master Poetic Devices Table -->\n  <div style=\"background: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; margin-bottom: 24px;\">\n    <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; margin: 0 0 16px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700;\">3. Master Literary & Poetic Devices Table</h3>\n    <div style=\"overflow-x: auto;\">\n      <table style=\"width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 14px; text-align: left;\">\n        <thead>\n          <tr style=\"background: rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.15); border-bottom: 2px solid #FF9100;\">\n            <th style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #FF9100;\">Poetic Device</th>\n            <th style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #FFFFFF;\">Example from Poem</th>\n            <th style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #CBD5E1;\">Poetic Significance & Explanation</th>\n          </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);\">\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; font-weight: bold; color: #FF9100;\">Transferred Epithet</td>\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #F1F5F9;\">\"polished traffic\"<br/>\"selfish cars\"</td>\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #CBD5E1;\">The sophistication, affluence, and callous selfishness of the affluent urban occupants are transferred onto their mechanical vehicles.</td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.4);\">\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; font-weight: bold; color: #FF9100;\">Oxymoron</td>\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #F1F5F9;\">\"greedy good-doers\"<br/>\"beneficent beasts of prey\"</td>\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #CBD5E1;\">Exposes the hypocrisy of social reformers, politicians, and capitalists who parade as charitable benefactors while systematically fleecing rural peasants.</td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);\">\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; font-weight: bold; color: #FF9100;\">Personification</td>\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #F1F5F9;\">\"roadside stand that too pathetically pled\"<br/>\"sadness that lurks near the open window\"</td>\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #CBD5E1;\">The wooden stall and the open window are imbued with human emotions of desperate begging and lingering sorrow, dramatizing their silent anguish.</td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.4);\">\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; font-weight: bold; color: #FF9100;\">Metaphor</td>\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #F1F5F9;\">\"flower of cities from sinking\"<br/>\"childish longing in vain\"</td>\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #CBD5E1;\">Compares the affluent luxury of metropolis to a delicate blooming blossom nurtured by financial capital; compares the farmers' fruitless optimism to a naive child's impossible wish.</td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);\">\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; font-weight: bold; color: #FF9100;\">Alliteration</td>\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #F1F5F9;\">\"greedy good-doers\"<br/>\"beneficent beasts\"<br/>\"cooling covert\"</td>\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #CBD5E1;\">Phonetic repetition creates rhythmic bite, emphasizing the poet's biting moral indictment of false philanthropists.</td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr>\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; font-weight: bold; color: #FF9100;\">Irony / Sarcasm</td>\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #F1F5F9;\">\"mercifully gathered in to live in villages\"<br/>\"by teaching them how to sleep they sleep all day\"</td>\n            <td style=\"padding: 10px 12px; color: #CBD5E1;\">Highlights how modern welfare destroys rural work ethic and self-reliance under the guise of paternalistic rehabilitation.</td>\n          </tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Vocabulary Glossary -->\n  <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border-left: 4px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0; padding: 18px 20px;\">\n    <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 700;\">4. Essential Stanza Vocabulary</h3>\n    <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; font-size: 13px;\">\n      <div><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">Dole of bread:</b> Humiliating handout or charitable crust.</div>\n      <div><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">Mar:</b> Spoil, disfigure, or damage the aesthetic beauty.</div>\n      <div><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">Pitiful kin:</b> Destitute rural relatives living in poverty.</div>\n      <div><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">Beneficent:</b> Seemingly charitable or well-meaning.</div>\n      <div><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">Soothe out of wits:</b> Stupefy into mindless passivity.</div>\n      <div><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">Quarts:</b> Traditional wooden dry volume measures.</div>\n      <div><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">Crook-necked:</b> Gourds/squash having bent, curved necks.</div>\n      <div><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">At one stroke:</b> In a single sudden, decisive, terminal action.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n";

export const c12EngF12HtmlSolutions = "\n<div style=\"padding: 16px; color: #F8FAFC; text-align: justify; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif; line-height: 1.85; font-size: 15px;\">\n\n  <!-- SECTION A: EXTRACT-BASED QUESTIONS -->\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom: 30px;\">\n    <div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25), rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.95)); border: 1.5px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px 18px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n      <h2 style=\"color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 800; margin: 0 0 4px 0;\">SECTION A: Extract-Based Questions (16 Marks)</h2>\n      <p style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0;\">Board Pattern: 4 Objective Extracts • 4 Questions Each • Continuous Q1 to Q16</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Extract 1 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.7); border-left: 4px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 18px; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n      <p style=\"font-style: italic; color: #E2E8F0; margin: 0 0 8px 0; font-size: 14px;\">\n        \"The little old house was out with a little new shed<br/>\n        In front at the edge of the road where the traffic sped,<br/>\n        A roadside stand that too pathetically pled,<br/>\n        It would not be fair to say for a dole of bread,<br/>\n        But for some of the money, the cash, whose flow supports<br/>\n        The flower of cities from sinking and withering faint.\"\n      </p>\n      <span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700;\">— Extract 1 (Stanza 1)</span>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q1 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q1: Where was the roadside stand located, and who had erected it?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> The roadside stand was built as a humble new wooden shed in front of an old cottage right at the edge of a bustling highway. It was erected by poor rural folk seeking to sell country produce to passing motorists.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q2 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q2: Why does the poet assert that it was not begging for a \"dole of bread\"?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> Frost clarifies that the owners were hardworking, dignified peasants, not beggars seeking humiliating charitable handouts (\"dole of bread\"). They were offering honest agricultural goods in return for hard currency through fair commerce.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q3 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q3: What role does money play in supporting the \"flower of cities\"?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> Liquid cash is the economic lifeblood of metropolitan centers. Just as water prevents a delicate flower from withering, steady monetary flow sustains the luxurious lifestyle, monuments, and culture of the urban elite.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q4 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 22px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q4: Identify the poetic device in \"A roadside stand that too pathetically pled\".</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> <b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">Personification</b>. The inanimate roadside shed is depicted as an emotional human being pathetically pleading with passing travelers for trade.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Extract 2 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.7); border-left: 4px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 18px; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n      <p style=\"font-style: italic; color: #E2E8F0; margin: 0 0 8px 0; font-size: 14px;\">\n        \"Here far from the city we make our roadside stand<br/>\n        And ask for some city money to feel in hand<br/>\n        To try if it will not make our being expand,<br/>\n        And give us the life of the moving-pictures' promise<br/>\n        That the party in power is said to be keeping from us.\"\n      </p>\n      <span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700;\">— Extract 2 (Stanza 2)</span>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q5 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q5: What do the roadside stand keepers hope to achieve by having \"city money in hand\"?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> They hope to elevate their impoverished living conditions (\"make our being expand\"). Having cash will allow them to buy modern necessities, improve their health, and experience personal dignity beyond bare rural subsistence.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q6 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q6: What is the \"moving-pictures' promise\"?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> It refers to the glamorous, comfortable, and affluent American dream portrayed in Hollywood cinema—a world of luxury, fine clothes, modern gadgets, and leisure that contrasts starkly with their gritty reality.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q7 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q7: What accusation is leveled against the \"party in power\"?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> The ruling political authorities are accused of deliberate betrayal and neglect—depriving rural citizens of basic development, public infrastructure, and economic opportunities that are showered exclusively upon cities.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q8 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 22px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q8: What produce does the roadside stand offer for sale?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> They offer wooden quarts of fresh wild berries, crook-necked golden squash with silver warts, and modest lodging to rest in peaceful mountain scenery.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Extract 3 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.7); border-left: 4px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 18px; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n      <p style=\"font-style: italic; color: #E2E8F0; margin: 0 0 8px 0; font-size: 14px;\">\n        \"It is in the news that all these pitiful kin<br/>\n        Are to be bought out and mercifully gathered in<br/>\n        To live in villages, next to the theatre and the store,<br/>\n        Where they won't have to think for themselves anymore,<br/>\n        While greedy good-doers, beneficent beasts of prey,<br/>\n        Swarm over their lives enforcing benefits...\"\n      </p>\n      <span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700;\">— Extract 3 (Stanza 3)</span>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q9 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q9: What news is circulating regarding the \"pitiful kin\"?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> Government reports declare that impoverished rural families will be bought out of their lands and relocated to planned suburban settlements adjacent to commercial stores and movie theaters.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q10 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q10: Explain the oxymoron in \"greedy good-doers\" and \"beneficent beasts of prey\".</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> These oxymorons expose fraudulent philanthropists and corrupt politicians who pose as noble social benefactors ('good-doers', 'beneficent') while actually acting as ruthless predators ('greedy', 'beasts of prey') exploiting rural helplessness for financial and political gain.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q11 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q11: How do these enforced benefits affect the villagers' way of life?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> The enforced welfare schemes numb their critical thinking and rob them of ancestral independence. By conditioning them to rely on state handouts, the planners lull them into lethargy and destroy their industrious habits.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q12 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 22px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q12: What does \"where they won't have to think for themselves anymore\" imply?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> It carries biting sarcasm. The state reduces independent agrarian citizens into brainwashed, passive consumers who are stripped of self-determination and critical discernment.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Extract 4 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.7); border-left: 4px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 18px; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n      <p style=\"font-style: italic; color: #E2E8F0; margin: 0 0 8px 0; font-size: 14px;\">\n        \"Sometimes I feel myself I can hardly bear<br/>\n        The thought of so much childish longing in vain,<br/>\n        The sadness that lurks near the open window there,<br/>\n        That waits all day in almost open prayer<br/>\n        For the squeal of brakes, the sound of a stopping car...\"\n      </p>\n      <span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700;\">— Extract 4 (Stanza 4)</span>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q13 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q13: What is the \"childish longing in vain\" that Frost refers to?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> It refers to the naive, persistent hope of the farmers waiting all day for speeding cars to stop and buy their goods. Like innocent children expecting impossible miracles, their longing is continually shattered by the indifference of the passing motorists.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q14 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q14: For what sound does the open window wait all day in prayer?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> The open window yearns to hear the \"squeal of brakes\"—the sound of a car pulling over to the roadside stand to patronize their humble enterprise.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q15 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q15: When cars do stop, what selfish reasons do the drivers have?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> The rare cars stop only to execute a U-turn using the farmer's grass, to inquire directions to their destination, or to crossly demand gallons of gas that the rustic stall does not stock.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q16 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 22px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q16: Identify the poetic device in \"sadness that lurks near the open window\".</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> <b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">Personification</b>. Sadness is personified as a ghostly human presence waiting silently by the windowsill in prayerful expectation.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- SECTION B: SHORT ANSWER QUESTIONS -->\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom: 30px;\">\n    <div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25), rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.95)); border: 1.5px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px 18px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n      <h2 style=\"color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 800; margin: 0 0 4px 0;\">SECTION B: Short Answer Questions (3 Marks • 40–50 Words)</h2>\n      <p style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0;\">Board Standard: Analytical & Social Reasoning • 12 Questions (Q17 to Q28)</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q17 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border-left: 3px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q17: Why do the city motorists feel irritated when they look at the roadside stand?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> Motorists complain that the makeshift wooden shack and clumsily painted directional signs (with 'N' and 'S' turned wrong) disfigure the picturesque natural scenery. They are absorbed in aesthetic pretension while remaining blind to rural poverty.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q18 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border-left: 3px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q18: What is the \"sorrow of what is unsaid\" in the poem?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> The unsaid sorrow is the deep humiliation felt by the peasants when city travellers look down on them. It is the unexpressed heartache of offering honest labor only to be treated with scorn, neglect, and disgust by their affluent countrymen.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q19 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border-left: 3px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q19: How does Frost use the phrase \"polished traffic\" as a transferred epithet?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> The word \"polished\" literally refers to the sleek, gleaming finish of high-end cars, but Frost transfers it to describe the sophisticated, calloused, and self-absorbed minds of the urban elite driving them.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q20 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border-left: 3px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q20: Why are the social reformers described as \"beneficent beasts of prey\"?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> Though they pose as beneficent philanthropists bringing welfare projects, they are predators targeting rural lands and votes. Their paternalistic schemes rob villagers of self-reliance while enriching real-estate and corporate interests.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q21 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border-left: 3px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q21: How do modern welfare schemes \"destroy their practice... the ancient way\"?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> For generations, rural folk survived by disciplined physical toil and agrarian rhythms (\"the ancient way\"). By showering them with passive entertainment and handouts, reformers destroy their stamina and pride in productive work.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q22 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border-left: 3px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q22: What does the poet mean by \"country scale of gain\"?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> It refers to the meager, subsistence-level monetary turnover of the rural economy. In the country scale, financial gains are negligible, never providing the economic leap needed to elevate spirit or living standards.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q23 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border-left: 3px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q23: Why does a motorist stop to ask for a gallon of gas?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> The driver stops out of thoughtless entitlement without observing the rustic nature of the stall. His absurd demand reveals utter ignorance of rural realities, followed by irritated impatience when turned down.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q24 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border-left: 3px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q24: What momentary thought does Frost express about ending the villagers' pain?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> Overcome by agonizing compassion, Frost momentarily contemplates that it would be a mercy to put these suffering people out of their misery \"at one stroke\" (euthanasia), freeing them from endless starvation and neglect.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q25 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border-left: 3px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q25: Why does Frost retract his radical thought the next day?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> On regaining moral composure, Frost recognizes that eliminating the sufferers rather than solving systemic injustice is horrifying. He realizes he would never want someone to execute him to end his own emotional anguish.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q26 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border-left: 3px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q26: What contrast does the poet draw between the city and country lifestyles?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> The city enjoys immense capital, cinematic glamour, leisure, and political favoritism. In contrast, the countryside endures crushing poverty, neglected public services, and economic marginalization.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q27 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border-left: 3px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q27: How does Frost capture the physical posture of waiting at the stand?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> He evokes an open window where sorrow lingers in \"almost open prayer\" throughout the day, vividly depicting the weary farmers staring persistently at the highway, straining to hear braking tires.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q28 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border-left: 3px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 22px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q28: What is the central plea of Robert Frost through this poem?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> Frost appeals for genuine economic parity, active empathy, and dignified commercial inclusion for rural producers, demanding that the wealthy share national wealth through fair trade rather than condescending charity.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- SECTION C: LONG ANSWER QUESTIONS -->\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom: 30px;\">\n    <div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25), rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.95)); border: 1.5px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px 18px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n      <h2 style=\"color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 800; margin: 0 0 4px 0;\">SECTION C: Long Analytical Questions (6 Marks • 120–150 Words)</h2>\n      <p style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0;\">3-Tier Model: Rural Crisis Context • Exploitation & Irony • Ethical Conclusion • Q29 to Q34</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q29 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.3); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px; margin-bottom: 18px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 10px 0;\">Q29: Discuss the rural-urban economic divide in \"A Roadside Stand\" and explain how Frost indicts the callousness of the urban elite.</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span></p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">1. Context & Structural Disparity:</b> Robert Frost highlights the deep economic chasm between booming urban centers and destitute agrarian settlements. The rustic roadside stand, set up along a speeding highway, pathetically pleads not for charitable handouts, but for a share of the liquid cash that nurtures the \"flower of cities\". While urban centers thrive on national resources, rural communities remain starved of capital and basic public amenities.</p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">2. The Callousness of \"Polished Traffic\":</b> City travellers speed past with cold indifference. Rather than buying fresh berries or golden squash, they complain that the crude shack and handmade signs with backward letters disfigure the natural scenery. Even when vehicles stop, their intent is purely self-serving: executing U-turns on the farmer's lawn, demanding travel directions, or requesting gasoline that the stall clearly does not stock.</p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">3. Critical Conclusion:</b> Frost exposes the moral bankruptcy of affluent urbanites who fetishize scenic beauty while remaining blind to the misery of the very people whose toil sustains their food supply.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q30 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.3); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px; margin-bottom: 18px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 10px 0;\">Q30: Critically examine Frost's attack on \"greedy good-doers\" and government resettlement programs.</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span></p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">1. Paternalistic Exploitation:</b> Frost unleashes sharp satire against opportunistic politicians, real estate tycoons, and corporate reformers who present themselves as benevolent benefactors. He labels them with stinging oxymorons: \"greedy good-doers\" and \"beneficent beasts of prey\". These groups swarm over rural communities to enforce government resettlement plans under the guise of compassion.</p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">2. Destruction of Self-Reliance:</b> The plan to move villagers into suburban clusters next to retail outlets and cinema halls aims to seize fertile ancestral lands for commercial development. By conditioning peasants to rely on state doles, the reformers \"soothe them out of their wits\". They erode the farmers' traditional work ethic (\"ancient way\"), replacing self-sufficient pride with passive dependency.</p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">3. Critical Conclusion:</b> Frost demonstrates that institutional welfare often serves as an instrument of social control, stripping marginalized communities of their land, heritage, and human dignity.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q31 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.3); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px; margin-bottom: 18px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 10px 0;\">Q31: Analyze the emotional trajectory of the poet, culminating in his shocking contemplation of \"at one stroke\" putting them out of pain.</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span></p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">1. The Burden of Empathy:</b> Frost's tone moves from conversational irony to unbearable personal grief as he witnesses the farmers' \"childish longing in vain\". Watching the open window wait all day in mute prayer for a car to stop causes him visceral pain, making him identify deeply with their crushed hopes.</p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">2. The Radical Impulse:</b> Pushed to the brink of despair, Frost confesses that it would bring great relief to end their misery \"at one stroke\" through euthanasia. This shocking thought is not born of cruelty, but of profound anguish at the slow starvation and humiliation endured daily by the rustic families.</p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">3. Moral Self-Correction:</b> The next morning, reason and ethical sanity prevail. Frost recoils from his dark thought, wondering how he would feel if someone offered to terminate his own life to relieve his grief. This reversal underscores the poet's belief in the sanctity of human life and the urgent need for systemic social justice rather than fatalistic resignation.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q32 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.3); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px; margin-bottom: 18px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 10px 0;\">Q32: Explain the significance of the \"moving-pictures' promise\" and its political betrayal.</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span></p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">1. The Cinematic Illusion:</b> The \"moving-pictures' promise\" represents the glamorous vision of the American Dream popularized by early cinema—a life filled with modern comfort, fine clothes, personal agency, and upward social mobility. For rural people living in grinding poverty, cinema screens offered a tantalizing glimpse of prosperity.</p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">2. Political Neglect:</b> Frost points out that this promise has been deliberately withheld by the \"party in power\". Ruling elites make grandiose campaign pledges to bring electrification, roads, and prosperity to the hinterland, only to abandon the peasantry once elections are concluded.</p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">3. Critical Conclusion:</b> Frost highlights the cruel psychological betrayal experienced by rural citizens, whose exposure to media highlights their poverty while institutional neglect keeps real progress out of reach.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q33 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.3); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px; margin-bottom: 18px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 10px 0;\">Q33: How does Robert Frost employ irony, transferred epithets, and personification to convey his message?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span></p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">1. Personification & Transferred Epithets:</b> Frost imbues inanimate objects with human emotion. The roadside stand \"pathetically pled\", while sadness \"lurks near the open window\" waiting in prayer. Transferred epithets like \"polished traffic\" and \"selfish cars\" transfer the cold, self-absorbed mindset of the urban elite onto their vehicles.</p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">2. Biting Irony & Oxymorons:</b> Irony permeates the depiction of motorists complaining about misspelled signs while remaining blind to starvation. Frost deepens this with oxymorons like \"greedy good-doers\" and \"beneficent beasts of prey\", exposing the hypocrisy of predatory politicians who masquerade as charitable reformers.</p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">3. Critical Conclusion:</b> These literary devices sharpen the emotional resonance of the poem, transforming a simple roadside scene into a profound indictment of socioeconomic inequality.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q34 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.3); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px; margin-bottom: 22px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 10px 0;\">Q34: Evaluate \"A Roadside Stand\" as an urgent appeal for human dignity and economic justice.</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span></p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">1. Dignity over Charity:</b> At its core, the poem champions human dignity. The stand owners do not seek degrading hand-outs (\"dole of bread\"); they seek an equitable economic relationship through honest trade. They offer authentic, homegrown produce in exchange for fair remuneration.</p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">2. The Cry for Economic Inclusion:</b> Frost argues that true national progress cannot be built on the exploitation of rural communities. Denying farmers access to capital and public services reduces them to second-class citizens, while paternalistic welfare only perpetuates their subjugation.</p>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0;\"><b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">3. Enduring Relevance:</b> The poem remains a timeless reminder that genuine solidarity lies in extending dignity, fair economic partnerships, and respect to those whose labor quietly sustains society.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- SECTION D: NCERT TEXTBOOK EXERCISES -->\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n    <div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25), rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.95)); border: 1.5px solid #FF9100; border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px 18px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n      <h2 style=\"color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 800; margin: 0 0 4px 0;\">SECTION D: NCERT Textbook Exercises (Thinking About The Poem)</h2>\n      <p style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0;\">Official Curriculum Solutions • Questions Q35 to Q38</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q35 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q35: The city folk who drove through the countryside hardly paid any heed to the roadside stand or to the people who ran it. If at all they did, it was to complain. Which lines bring this out? What was their complaint about?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> The lines are: <i>\"The polished traffic passed with a mind ahead, / Or if ever aside a moment, then out of sorts / At having the mar of the landscape with the artless paint / Of signs that with N turned wrong and S turned wrong.\"</i> Their complaint was aesthetic: they were annoyed that the rustic wooden stand and crudely painted directional signs spoiled the natural beauty of the landscape.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q36 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q36: What was the plea of the folk who had put up the roadside stand?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> The plea of the rural folk was not for a degrading \"dole of bread\" (charity). Rather, they pleaded for some \"city money\" through honest trade, seeking to earn cash by selling wild berries and squash so they could improve their living conditions and enjoy the prosperity promised by modern society.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q37 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q37: The government and other social service agencies appear to help the poor rural people, but do them no good. Pick out the words and phrases that the poet uses to show their double standards.</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> Frost exposes their hypocrisy through striking phrases such as: <b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">\"greedy good-doers\"</b>, <b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">\"beneficent beasts of prey\"</b>, and <b style=\"color: #FF9100;\">\"enforcing benefits that are calculated to soothe them out of their wits\"</b>. These phrases show that government authorities and commercial reformers exploit rural simplicity under the facade of charitable assistance.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Q38 -->\n    <div style=\"background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 145, 0, 0.25); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px;\">\n      <h3 style=\"color: #FF9100; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Q38: What is the 'childish longing' that the poet refers to? Why is it 'in vain'?</h3>\n      <p style=\"margin: 0 0 6px 0;\"><span style=\"color: #FF9100; font-weight: bold;\">✓ Answer:</span> The 'childish longing' refers to the persistent, innocent hope of the roadside vendors who wait all day by the open window for speeding cars to stop and buy their goods. It is 'in vain' because out of thousands of passing vehicles, almost none stop to purchase produce; those that do stop only seek directions, make U-turns, or demand gasoline.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n</div>\n";

